    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a093ccee-e58d-5a14-9fe5-261bbeb1350a",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is not invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=5 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\n$det(A)=0$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<5$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{5}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $A\\text{ is not invertible}$. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true: $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$. $\\text{rank}(A)<5$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\n- Statement III is false: $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and II only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
